  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. Clean combinations and the multiplicity spaces\n**Observation from Section 6.** The ratios are $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent up to $O(\\varepsilon)$, so the leading contamination is structural. For $[4,4,0]$, both $[4,3,1]$ copies and $[4,2,2]$, the $d_{(1,1)}$ and $d_{(2,2)}$ contaminations stand in the fixed ratio $2:3$. Hence\n$$v_1=3\\,d_{(1,1)}-2\\,d_{(2,2)}$$\nshould be clean on all four. $[3,3,2]$ is different: only $d_{(3,2)}$ has a signal there, and its contamination vector is not of that form.\n\nThis cell gives $\\kappa(v_1)$ on all states. It then tests the rank of the clean functionals restricted to the 2-dimensional HW spaces of $[5,2,1]$ and $[4,3,1]$ as $w$ varies. The rows are the covectors at 5 values of $\\omega$, restricted to $P_{\\rm HW}$, and the table lists their relative singular values at two $\\varepsilon$. A second singular value that shrinks like $\\varepsilon$ means the leading-order rank is 1.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* covector of a top-killed combination with coefficients cf on the shapes, at twists (zv, wv) *)\ncovTK[cf_, zv_, wv_] := Sum[cf[[j]] With[{c = cλ[locShapes[[j]], zv, wv]}, c - (c . kron[e1, e1]) kron[e1, e1]], {j, Length[cf]}];\nvFrom[cf_, d_] := Sum[cf[[j]] topKill[j, d], {j, Length[cf]}];\nv1cf = {3, -2, 0};\nκV1 = Table[{μc[[1]], μc[[2]], κv[vFrom[v1cf, KSm[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[1]]]], KSm[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[1]]]], κv[vFrom[v1cf, KSm[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[2]]]], KSm[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], εs[[2]]]]}, {μc, hwList}];\nωSet = {ω, {1/9, 5/4, -3/7}, {-3/5, 2/7, 1/3}, {5/6, 1/2, -1/8}, {2/9, -7/10, 3/4}};\n(* relative singular values of {cov(w)} restricted to HW_μ, for a list of coefficient vectors *)\nhwRank[μ_, cfs_, ε_] := Module[{zv = N[Exp[ε φ], pr], m}, m = Flatten[Table[hwB[μ] . covTK[cf, zv, N[Exp[ε ωv], pr]], {cf, cfs}, {ωv, ωSet}], 1]; N[SingularValueList[m, Tolerance -> 0]/Norm[m], 3]];\nd1cfs = {{1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}};\n{tR7, rk7} = AbsoluteTiming[{\n    {\"[5,2,1]: d11, d22, d32, five w\", hwRank[{5, 2, 1}, d1cfs, 10^-4], hwRank[{5, 2, 1}, d1cfs, 10^-5]},\n    {\"[5,2,1]: d11 only, five w\", hwRank[{5, 2, 1}, {{1, 0, 0}}, 10^-4], hwRank[{5, 2, 1}, {{1, 0, 0}}, 10^-5]},\n    {\"[4,3,1]: v1 only, five w\", hwRank[{4, 3, 1}, {v1cf}, 10^-4], hwRank[{4, 3, 1}, {v1cf}, 10^-5]}}];\nColumn[{Grid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"κ(v1), ε=10^-3\", \"ε=10^-4\"}}, κV1], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Join[{{\"functionals\", \"rel. singular values, ε=10^-4\", \"ε=10^-5\"}}, rk7, {{\"time (s)\", tR7, \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
