  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results for $[3,1,0]^2$ with site-1 data + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ only (2026-10-02, P1, $\\varepsilon\\le10^{-4}$, 120 digits)\n- **Checks.** Localization of $T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,2)},T_{(3,2)}(\\theta_1-3h)$ holds to more than $10^{-106}$. The chain residual is $\\sim10^{-90}$. $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ equals the top component of $(R\\otimes R)\\Psi_\\perp$ to $\\sim10^{-78}$.\n- **Top-killing ($d_\\lambda=c_\\lambda-(c_\\lambda\\cdot e_1e_1)c_0$) is enough for** $[6,1,1]$ (via $d_{(3,2)}$), $[5,3,0]$ and both $[5,2,1]$ (each $d_\\lambda$ separately).\n- **Not enough for the deep states.** $[4,4,0]$ has $\\kappa=t$ for both $d_{(2,2)}$ and $d_{(3,2)}$. Both $[4,3,1]$, $[4,2,2]$ and $[3,3,2]$ also keep contamination. All their ratios are $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent to $O(\\varepsilon)$, so the contamination is structural.\n- **One universal combination, $v_1=3d_{(1,1)}-2d_{(2,2)}$,** gives $\\kappa\\to1$ on $[5,3,0]$, $[5,2,1]_{1,2}$, $[4,4,0]$, $[4,3,1]_{1,2}$ and $[4,2,2]$. On $[3,3,2]$ it has CG $=0$; only $d_{(3,2)}$ sees $[3,3,2]$.\n- **$[5,2,1]$ mixing is fixed.** $d_{(1,1)},d_{(2,2)},d_{(3,2)}$ over five $w$ have rank 2 on its HW space (second singular value $\\approx0.13$).\n- **$[4,3,1]$ mixing is not fixed by these data.** The two copies' contamination vectors force any combination that is clean on both to be $\\propto v_1$, and $v_1$ restricted to the $[4,3,1]$ HW space has a $w$-independent direction (rank exactly 1 over five $w$, at both $\\varepsilon$). A single $d_\\lambda$ also has a fixed direction on its HW space.\n- **$[3,3,2]$.** It has multiplicity 1, so only its normalization is at stake. A clean combination exists (one linear condition on $d_{(1,1)},d_{(2,2)},d_{(3,2)}$), but its coefficients have not been identified in closed form.\n- **Open.** Add the site-2 covectors and redo the constraint analysis for $[4,3,1]$. Alternatively, test whether per-state clean combinations, with coefficients depending on the state's transfer eigenvalues, give rank 2.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Adding the site-2 insertions\n$A=t_2(\\theta_2+h)$ and $B=t_2(\\theta_2+h)\\,t_1(\\theta_2-h)$ localize on site 2 (`L2-310-localization.md`). For any insertion $X$ built from $t$'s, $\\langle\\Omega|X|\\Psi\\rangle=X^B\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$, which is a Q-side number. Its covector in the frame with $R$ undone is $c_X=\\langle\\Omega|X\\,(R\\otimes R)^{-1}$. Here $c_X$ is computed numerically from the operators, so the site-2 prefactors are not needed. Locality on site 2 shows up as $c_X=e_1^T\\otimes(\\cdot)$, and that is checked.\n\nThe basis is now $\\{c_0;\\ c_{(1,1)},c_{(2,2)},c_{(3,2)};\\ c_A,c_B\\}$. As before, everything is top-killed: $d_X=c_X-(c_X\\cdot e_1e_1)c_0$. Per state, $k$ and $s$ are the contamination and signal of the five $d$'s, both divided by the signal of $d_{(3,2)}$. The first table tests whether these ratios are structural, i.e. independent of the twist directions.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "site2Ops[zv_] := With[{Z = DiagonalMatrix[zv], u2 = thN[[2]]}, {tL2[2, u2 + hN, Z], tL2[2, u2 + hN, Z] . tL2[1, u2 - hN, Z]}];\nlabels2 = Join[ToString /@ locShapes, {\"A\", \"B\"}]; nD = Length[labels2];\n(* the five top-killed covectors at twists (zv, wv): site-1 from the closed form, site 2 as <Ω|X (R⊗R)^-1 *)\ndCovs[zv_, wv_] := Module[{RRi = With[{g = RrotInv[zv, wv]}, KroneckerProduct[g, g]], cs},\n   cs = Join[cλ[#, zv, wv] & /@ locShapes, ((Om2[zv, wv] . #) . RRi) & /@ site2Ops[zv]];\n   (# - (# . kron[e1, e1]) kron[e1, e1]) & /@ cs];\nKS2[μ_, copy_, ε_, φv_, ωv_] := Module[{zv = N[Exp[ε φv], pr], wv = N[Exp[ε ωv], pr], Ψ, Ψhw, rest, ds, k},\n   Ψ = pickState[μ, copy, zv][\"psi\"]; Ψhw = projHW[μ, Ψ]; rest = RR[zv, wv] . (Ψ - Ψhw); ds = dCovs[zv, wv];\n   <|\"S\" -> (# . Ψhw & /@ ds), \"K\" -> (# . rest & /@ ds), \"sc\" -> Norm[Ψ] Max[Norm /@ ds]|>];\nKS2m[μ_, copy_, ε_] := KS2m[μ, copy, ε] = KS2[μ, copy, ε, φ, ω];\nnormKS[d_] := With[{sref = d[\"S\"][[Length[locShapes]]]}, {d[\"K\"]/sref, d[\"S\"]/sref}];\n(* checks: site-2 covectors are e1 ⊗ (·) (only site-1 row 1 nonzero) *)\nloc2Res = With[{ds = dCovs[zT, wT], Ri = With[{g = RrotInv[zT, wT]}, KroneckerProduct[g, g]]}, Table[With[{c = (Om2[zT, wT] . X) . Ri}, maxAbs[Partition[c, d1][[2 ;;]]]/maxAbs[c]], {X, site2Ops[zT]}]];\n(* structural test: spread of k and s over three direction pairs, ε = 10^-5 *)\nnonTop = Rest[hwList];\n{tS2, struct2} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{r = Table[normKS[KS2[μc[[1]], μc[[2]], 10^-5, dd[[2]], dd[[3]]]], {dd, dirs}]},\n     {μc[[1]], μc[[2]], N[Max[Table[Max[Abs[Flatten[r[[i]] - r[[1]]]]], {i, Length[r]}]], 2], N[Re[r[[1, 1]]], 5], N[Re[r[[1, 2]]], 5]}], {μc, nonTop}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"copy\", \"spread over directions\", \"k = K_j/S_ref, j = \" <> ToString[labels2], \"s = S_j/S_ref\"}}, struct2,\n   {{\"site-2 locality residual (A, B)\", N[loc2Res, 3], \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"time (s)\", tS2, \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"942214\" data-output-id=\"61\" data-out-n=\"662\" data-sub-idx=\"12\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"18\" data-sub-start=\"17\" data-sub-end=\"18\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[662]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"26\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:14.54em;vertical-align:-7em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.54em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:9.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:14.5em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-7em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.5em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.66em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose delimcent