       "data": "Out[671]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\mu  & \\text{copy} & \\text{mult} & \\text{rel. error of a, $\\varepsilon$=10\\^{}-4} & \\text{angle error, $\\varepsilon$=10\\^{}-4} & \\text{rel. error, $\\varepsilon$=10\\^{}-5} & \\text{angle error, $\\varepsilon$=10\\^{}-5}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{6,1,1\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 2.01\\times 10^{-14} & 0.\\times 10^{-44} & 0 & 0.\\times 10^{-44}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{5,3,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 4.85\\times 10^{-11} & 0.\\times 10^{-42} & 0 & 0.\\times 10^{-42}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{5,2,1\\right\\} & 1 & 2 & 4.58\\times 10^{-6} & 3.54\\times 10^{-6} & 4.58\\times 10^{-7} & 3.54\\times 10^{-7}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{5,2,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.0000607 & 0.0000322 & 6.07\\times 10^{-6} & 3.22\\times 10^{-6}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,4,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0.0000395 & 0.\\times 10^{-43} & 0 & 0.\\times 10^{-41}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,3,1\\right\\} & 1 & 2 & 8.99\\times 10^{-6} & 3.55\\times 10^{-6} & 1.42\\times 10^{-6} & 9.07\\times 10^{-7}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,3,1\\right\\} & 2 & 2 & 0.0000322 & 0.0000142 & 3.76\\times 10^{-6} & 7.46\\times 10^{-7}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{4,2,2\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0.0000641 & 0.\\times 10^{-38} & 8.70\\times 10^{-6} & 0.\\times 10^{-35}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{3,3,2\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & 0.0000227 & 0.\\times 10^{-33} & 6.90\\times 10^{-6} & 0.\\times… [latex truncated: 1278 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "4a084917-1e78-47b7-922a-23911dcd5dac"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results of Section 8 (2026-10-02, P1, 120 digits)\n- **Site-2 insertions.** $A$ and $B$ are exactly site-2 local, $c_X=e_1^T\\otimes(\\cdot)$, to $10^{-112}$. With them included, every contamination ratio, for all 9 non-top HW states and all five insertions, is $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent to $O(\\varepsilon)$.\n- **Clean spaces.** They have dimension 4 for each multiplicity-1 sector and 3 for $[5,2,1]$ and $[4,3,1]$, out of 5 top-killed insertions. Restricted to the HW space over five $w$, the clean covectors have **rank 2 on both $[5,2,1]$ and $[4,3,1]$**. The second singular values, $\\approx0.16$ and $0.05$, do not shrink with $\\varepsilon$. Site-1 data alone gave rank 1 on $[4,3,1]$, so $A,B$ supply the missing direction.\n- **End to end.** From the Q-side numbers alone (eigenvalue $\\times\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ minus the top part), least squares over the clean combinations recovers $P_{\\rm HW}\\Psi_B$, **scale included**, for all 9 non-top HW states. $[6,2,0]$ is trivial.\n  - Direction errors on $[5,2,1]$ and $[4,3,1]$: $\\sim10^{-5}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-4}$, $\\lesssim10^{-6}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$.\n  - Scale errors: $\\lesssim10^{-5}$.\n  - So **site 1 + site 2 + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ fixes all the CG data of $[3,1,0]^2$** with clean leading-order functionals, with no full-vector reconstruction.\n- **Caveats.**\n  - The clean spaces were obtained numerically from the states' own contamination vectors at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$. These are structural, but **not yet in closed form** (compare $\\beta(t)$ for $[2,1,0]$). That is also why the errors at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$ partly plateau ($[3,3,2]$, $[4,2,2]$).\n  - One chain point only.\n  - The eigenvalues are read from the eigenvectors and stand in for the Q's.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. Site 1 only, with per-copy cleaning\nSection 7 found that site 1 + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ fails on $[4,3,1]$ with *sector-wide* cleaning: the only combination clean on both copies is $v_1$, which has rank 1 there. Here each copy is allowed its own clean combinations, from the null space of that copy's constraint alone, as was needed for $[6,4,2]$ in $[4,2,0]^2$. Only the three site-1 insertions are used. A sector uses the sector-wide space where that has full HW rank, and per-copy spaces otherwise. Fair test: clean spaces fitted at $(\\varepsilon=10^{-5},\\varphi,\\omega)$, and errors of the recovered $P_{\\rm HW}\\Psi$ (scale included) at $(10^{-4},\\varphi)$ and $(10^{-5},\\varphi')$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "sub1 = Range[Length[locShapes]];\nembed5[v_] := Join[v, ConstantArray[0, nD - Length[v]]];\n(* k is normalized by a signal, so a genuinely contaminated k is O(1); a k below 10^-2 is O(ε) noise and imposes no constraint (a relative cut would discard the clean insertion itself) *)\nkTol = 10^-2;\nnullOf[rows_] := With[{rr = Select[rows, Norm[#] > kTol &]}, If[rr === {}, IdentityMatrix[Length[sub1]],\n    Module[{sv = SingularValueList[rr, Tolerance -> 0], r, V}, r = Count[sv, x_ /; x > 10^-3 Max[sv]]; V = SingularValueDecomposition[rr][[3]]; Transpose[V][[r + 1 ;;]]]]];\ncleanSec1[μ_] := embed5 /@ nullOf[Table[normKS[KS2m[μ, c, 10^-5]][[1, sub1]], {c, Length[hwB[μ]]}]];\ncleanCopy1[μ_, c_] := embed5 /@ nullOf[{normKS[KS2m[μ, c, 10^-5]][[1, sub1]]}];\nreconV[μ_, copy_, ε_, vs_, φv_] := Module[{zv = N[Exp[ε φv], pr], Ψ, M, y, a, tru, re}, Ψ = pickState[μ, copy, zv][\"psi\"];\n   {M, y} = Transpose[Flatten[Table[With[{wv = N[Exp[ε ωv], pr]}, With[{ds = dCovs[zv, wv], q = qNums[Ψ, zv, wv]}, Table[{hwB[μ] . (v . ds), v . q}, {v, vs}]]], {ωv, ωSet}], 1]];\n   a = LeastSquares[M, y]; tru = hwB[μ] . Ψ; re = Norm[a - tru]/Norm[tru]; {N[re, 3], Round[Precision[re]]}];\nφp = {-2/5, 3/8, 7/11};\n{t9, tab9} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[Module[{mult = Length[hwB[μ]], cs, rk, full},\n     cs = cleanSec1[μ]; rk = Take[hwRank2[μ, cs, 10^-5], UpTo[mult + 1]];\n     full = Length[rk] >= mult && rk[[mult]] > 10^-3;\n     {μ, mult, Length[cs], rk, Table[With[{vs = If[full, cs, cleanCopy1[μ, c]]}, {If[full, \"sector\", \"per copy\"], reconV[μ, c, 10^-4, vs, φ], reconV[μ, c, 10^-5, vs, φp]}], {c, mult}]}], {μ, Rest[hwSecs]}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"mult\", \"dim sector clean (site 1)\", \"sector HW rel. sv (ε=10^-5)\", \"per copy: {space, {rel. err, digits} at (10^-4, φ), at (10^-5, φ')}\"}}, tab9, {{\"time (s)\", t9, \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"942214\" data-output-id=\"66\" data-out-n=\"697\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"25\" data-sub-start=\"16\" data-sub-end=\"16\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[697]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"27\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:13.355em;vertical-align:-6.4075em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.9475em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.9075em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.9075em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:13.315em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-6.4075em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.9075em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.5275em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.46em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.3125em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.46em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</s