  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results of Section 9 (2026-10-02, P1, 120 digits)\nWith **site 1 + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ only** (no site-2 insertions), all 9 non-top HW states of $[3,1,0]^2$ are recovered, scale included. Relative errors are $\\sim10^{-4}$–$10^{-5}$ at $(\\varepsilon=10^{-4},\\varphi)$ and $\\sim10^{-5}$–$10^{-6.5}$ at $(10^{-5},\\varphi')$, i.e. $O(\\varepsilon)$, with $\\ge62$ correct digits.\n- **Sector-wide cleaning is enough** for $[6,1,1]$, $[5,3,0]$, $[5,2,1]$ (rank 2), $[4,4,0]$, $[4,2,2]$ and $[3,3,2]$.\n- **$[4,3,1]$ needs per-copy cleaning.** The sector-wide clean space is 1-dimensional ($v_1$, rank 1), but each copy's own 2-dimensional clean space suffices.\n- **The price.** Per-copy coefficients depend on that copy's contamination ratios, so a closed form must involve the copy's own spectral data, e.g. its transfer eigenvalues. Section 8's site-2 insertions avoid that for $[4,3,1]$.\n- **Numerical fix.** An insertion that is already clean has $k=O(\\varepsilon)$. That noise must not be imposed as a constraint, hence the absolute cut `kTol`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 10. The site-1 eigenvalues in terms of dual Q's\n**Claim.** Write $v(u)=(Q^1,Q^2,Q^3)(u)$ for the dual Q's of a state, with $Q^j=z_j^{u/h}q^j$, $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$, solving the dual Baxter equation. Then, for $\\lambda_3=0$ and $\\lambda_1\\le\\Lambda_1$,\n$$T_\\lambda(\\theta_1-\\Lambda_1h)=P_\\lambda\\;\\frac{\\det_2\\big[v(\\theta_1+(\\lambda_1-\\Lambda_1)h),\\,v(\\theta_1+(\\lambda_2-\\Lambda_1-1)h)\\big]}{\\det_2\\big[v(\\theta_1-\\Lambda_1h),\\,v(\\theta_1-(\\Lambda_1+1)h)\\big]},\\qquad P_\\lambda=\\prod_{(r,c)\\in\\lambda}\\nu_3\\big(\\theta_1-\\Lambda_1h+(c-r)h\\big),$$\nwith $\\det_2$ any $2\\times2$ minor (the same rows top and bottom) and $\\nu_3(y)=\\prod_s(y-\\theta_s)$ the two-site factor. This is the L=1 \"reduction at $\\theta-2h$\" (clean write-up, row 13), with $2\\to\\Lambda_1$.\n\n**Derivation (to be tested).**\n- **Weyl formula.** $T_\\lambda(x)=P_\\lambda\\det[v(x+\\lambda_1h),v(x+(\\lambda_2-1)h),v(x-2h)]/\\det[v(x),v(x-h),v(x-2h)]$.\n- **3×3 Casoratian.** The dual Baxter equation gives $W(x)/W(x-h)=\\chi_3\\nu_1(x)\\nu_2(x-h)/(\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h))$ for $W(x)=\\det[v(x+h),v(x),v(x-h)]$. So $\\det[v(x),v(x-h),v(x-2h)]$ vanishes at $x=\\theta_s+h,\\dots,\\theta_s-(\\Lambda_1-1)h$.\n- **2×2 Casoratians (guess).** If the dual QQ relation carries $\\prod_{n=1}^{\\Lambda_2}(u-\\theta_s+nh)$, then $v(\\theta_s-\\Lambda_2h)\\parallel\\dots\\parallel v(\\theta_s)$.\n- **Together.** $v(\\theta_1-(\\Lambda_1+1)h),\\dots,v(\\theta_1)$ lie in one 2-plane. At $x=\\theta_1-\\Lambda_1h$ the common third column $v(\\theta_1-(\\Lambda_1+2)h)$ factors out of numerator and denominator.\n\n**For $[3,1,0]$ ($\\Lambda_1=3,\\Lambda_2=1$),** with $D_{ab}=\\det_2[v(\\theta_1-ah),v(\\theta_1-bh)]$ and $\\rho=Q^j(\\theta_1)/Q^j(\\theta_1-h)$ (the same for every $j$):\n- $T_{(1,1)}=P_{11}D_{23}/D_{34}$;\n- $T_{(2,2)}=P_{22}D_{12}/D_{34}$;\n- $T_{(3,2)}=P_{32}\\,\\rho\\,D_{12}/D_{34}$.\n\nThe cell solves the dual Baxter equation for every state of three weight sectors at the finite test twist, and checks the parallelism, the 2-plane, and the formula for all shapes with $\\lambda_1\\le3$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* eigenvalue polynomials t1 (deg 2), t2 (deg 4) of a state, by exact interpolation of the eigenvalue at 2a+1 points *)\ntEvPoly[Ψ_, zv_, a_] := Module[{k = Ordering[Abs[Ψ], -1][[1]], xs = Range[2 a + 1]/7}, InterpolatingPolynomial[Transpose[{xs, Table[(tL2[a, x, DiagonalMatrix[zv]] . Ψ)[[k]]/Ψ[[k]], {x, xs}]}], X]];\nt3Ev[zv_, x_] := (Times @@ zv) nu[1][x] nu[2][x - hN] nu[3][x - 2 hN];\n(* dual Baxter: ν3(x)ν3(x-h)ν3(x-2h)Q(x+h) - t1 ν3(x-h)ν3(x-2h)Q(x) + t2(x) ν3(x-2h)Q(x-h) - t3(x)Q(x-2h) = 0, Q = z^{x/h} q, q monic of degree d *)\ndualQ[zj_, d_, t1_, t2_] := Module[{c, q, eq, cl, sol},\n   q[x_] := x^d + Sum[c[i] x^i, {i, 0, d - 1}];\n   eq = Expand[nu[3][X] nu[3][X - hN] nu[3][X - 2 hN] zj q[X + hN] - t1 nu[3][X - hN] nu[3][X - 2 hN] q[X] + (t2 /. X -> X) nu[3][X - 2 hN] q[X - hN]/zj - t3Ev[zvCur, X] q[X - 2 hN]/zj^2];\n   cl = CoefficientList[eq, X];\n   sol = If[d == 0, {}, LeastSquares[Table[Coefficient[e, c[i]], {e, cl}, {i, 0, d - 1}], -(cl /. c[_] -> 0)]];\n   {Function[x, Evaluate[x^d + Sum[If[d == 0, 0, sol[[i + 1]]] x^i, {i, 0, d - 1}]]], Max[Abs[cl /. Thread[Table[c[i], {i, 0, d - 1}] -> sol]]]/Max[Abs[cl /. c[_] -> 0]]}];\n(* v(u) = (Q^1, Q^2, Q^3)(u) for a state of weight μ *)\nvQ[Ψ_, μ_, zv_] := Module[{t1 = tEvPoly[Ψ, zv, 1], t2 = tEvPoly[Ψ, zv, 2], qs},\n   zvCur = zv; qs = Table[dualQ[zv[[j]], μ[[j]], t1, t2], {j, 3}];\n   {Function[u, Evaluate[Table[zv[[j]]^(u/hN) qs[[j, 1]][u], {j, 3}]]], Max[qs[[All, 2]]]}];\ndet2[a_, b_, rows_] := a[[rows[[1]]]] b[[rows[[2]]]] - a[[rows[[2]]]] b[[rows[[1]]]];\nPlam[λ_] := Product[nu[3][uLoc + (c - r) hN], {r, Length[λ]}, {c, λ[[r]]}];\nΛ1 = Λ[[1]];\nshapes3 = Select[Flatten[Table[DeleteCases[{a, b}, 0], {a, 1, Λ1}, {b, 0, a}], 1], True &];\n(* tests for every state in a few sectors, finite twist zT *)\ntestSecs = {{5, 2, 1}, {4, 3, 1}, {3, 3, 2}};\n{t10, tests10} = AbsoluteTiming[Flatten[Table[Module[{sts = Select[statesAt[zT], #[\"mu\"] === μ &]}, Table[Module[{Ψ = st[\"psi\"], vv, res, v, th = thN[[1]], k, form, ev},\n       {vv, res} = vQ[Ψ, μ, zT]; v[n_] := vv[th - n hN];\n       k = Ordering[Abs[Ψ], -1][[1]];\n       form[λ_, rows_] := Plam[λ] det2[v[Λ1 - λ[[1]]], v[Λ1 + 1 - If[Length[λ] > 1, λ[[2]], 0]], rows]/det2[v[Λ1], v[Λ1 + 1], rows];\n       ev[λ_] := (TL2[λ, uLoc, DiagonalMatrix[zT]] . Ψ)[[k]]/Ψ[[k]];\n       {μ, res,\n        Max[Abs[Flatten[Table[det2[v[0], v[n], {1, 2}]/(Norm[v[0]] Norm[v[n]]), {n, 1, Λ[[2]]}]]]],\n        Max[Table[Abs[Det[{v[n], v[n + 1], v[n + 2]}]]/(Norm[v[n]] Norm[v[n + 1]] Norm[v[n + 2]]), {n, Λ[[2]], Λ1 - 1}]],\n        Abs[Det[{v[Λ1], v[Λ1 + 1], v[Λ1 + 2]}]]/(Norm[v[Λ1]] Norm[v[Λ1 + 1]] Norm[v[Λ1 + 2]]),\n        Max[Table[Abs[form[λ, rows] - ev[λ]]/Max[Abs[ev[λ]], 10^-30], {λ, shapes3}, {rows, {{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {1, 3}}}]]}], {st, sts}]], {μ, testSecs}], 1]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"μ\", \"dual Baxter residual\", \"parallel: max |det2[v(θ1), v(θ1-nh)]|, n≤Λ2 (rel.)\", \"plane: max |det3| of consecutive v in [θ1-(Λ1+1)h, θ1-Λ2 h] (rel.)\", \"|det3[v(θ1-Λ1h), v(-(Λ1+1)h), v(-(Λ1+2)h)]| (rel., should be ≠ 0)\", \"formula vs eigenvalue, all λ₁≤Λ₁ shapes and row pairs (max rel.)\"}},\n   Map[If[NumericQ[#], ScientificForm[N[#, 3], 3], #] &, tests10, {2}], {{\"time (s)\", t10, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
