   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result of Section 10 (2026-10-02, P1, finite test twist, 120 digits)\nThe check covers all 34 states of the sectors $(5,2,1)$, $(4,3,1)$ and $(3,3,2)$ (every state, not only HW-limit ones).\n- **Dual Q's.** Solved from the dual Baxter equation with $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$. Residual $\\le10^{-100}$.\n- **Parallelism** $v(\\theta_1)\\parallel v(\\theta_1-h)$ ($\\Lambda_2=1$): $\\le10^{-100}$. This supports the guessed dual-QQ factor $\\prod_{n=1}^{\\Lambda_2}(u-\\theta_s+nh)$.\n- **2-plane:** consecutive $3\\times3$ determinants in $[\\theta_1-4h,\\theta_1-h]$ vanish to $10^{-115}$. The denominator $\\det[v(\\theta_1-3h),v(\\theta_1-4h),v(\\theta_1-5h)]$ is nonzero for every state.\n- **The formula** $T_\\lambda(\\theta_1-3h)=P_\\lambda\\det_2[v(\\theta_1+(\\lambda_1-3)h),v(\\theta_1+(\\lambda_2-4)h)]/\\det_2[v(\\theta_1-3h),v(\\theta_1-4h)]$ holds for **every** shape with $\\lambda_1\\le3$ and every row pair, to $\\le10^{-70}$.\n\nSo, writing $D_{ab}=\\det_2[v(\\theta_1-ah),v(\\theta_1-bh)]$ (any fixed row pair), $\\rho=Q^j(\\theta_1)/Q^j(\\theta_1-h)$ (the same for all $j$), and $P_\\lambda=\\prod_{\\rm boxes}\\nu_3(\\theta_1-3h+(c-r)h)$:\n- $T_{(1,1)}=P_{11}D_{23}/D_{34}$;\n- $T_{(2,2)}=P_{22}D_{12}/D_{34}$;\n- $T_{(3,2)}=P_{32}\\,\\rho\\,D_{12}/D_{34}$.\n\nThe site-1 Q-numbers are these times $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$, the $6\\times6$ determinant. For $[3,1,0]$ that determinant formula has **not** been validated: only the adjoint was done.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Appendix A. Which $T_\\lambda$ localize? An independent scan\nThis is an independent check of the input from `L2-310-localization.md`. For every CBR shape $\\lambda$ with $\\lambda_1\\le4$ and $\\lambda_3=0$, and every shift $u=\\theta_1+ch$ with $c=-6,\\dots,2$, compute $C=\\langle\\Omega|T_\\lambda(u)$ at the finite test twist. Shapes with $\\lambda_3>0$ are a scalar (quantum determinants) times a smaller shape at a shifted point, so they add nothing. Reshape $C$ as a $d\\times d$ matrix (rows are site 1). Then:\n- **site-1 local** means $C=v\\,\\Omega_{zw}^T$;\n- **nontrivial** means $v\\not\\parallel\\Omega_{zw}$;\n- **eigen** means $C\\propto\\Omega$.\n\nThe covector is built by acting on $\\langle\\Omega|$ term by term (vector times sparse matrix), with $t_3$ replaced by the quantum determinant.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ⟨Ω| T_λ(x) as a covector: CBR permutation sum, applied factor by factor to the covector *)\ntApply[cv_, a_, x_, Z_] := Which[a == 0, cv, a == 3, (Times @@ Diagonal[Z]) nu[1][x] nu[2][x - hN] nu[3][x - 2 hN] cv, True, cv . tL2[a, x, Z]];\ncovT[λ_, x_, Z_, c0_] := With[{lc = conj[λ], n = Max[λ]}, Sum[With[{as = Table[lc[[σ[[i]]]] + i - σ[[i]], {i, n}]},\n     If[Min[as] < 0 || Max[as] > 3, 0 c0, Signature[σ] Fold[tApply[#1, #2[[1]], #2[[2]], Z] &, c0, Table[{as[[i]], x + (i - 1) hN}, {i, n}]]]], {σ, Permutations[Range[n]]}]];\nlocClass[cv_, o_] := Module[{C = Partition[cv, d1], v, r1, r2, rEig},\n   If[maxAbs[cv] == 0, Return[\"zero\"]];\n   v = C . o/(o . o); r1 = Norm[Flatten[C - Outer[Times, v, o]]]/Norm[Flatten[C]];\n   r2 = Norm[Flatten[C - Outer[Times, o, o . C/(o . o)]]]/Norm[Flatten[C]];\n   rEig = Norm[v - (v . o/(o . o)) o]/Norm[v];\n   Which[r1 < 10^-60 && rEig < 10^-60, \"eigen\", r1 < 10^-60, \"SITE 1\", r2 < 10^-60, \"site 2\", True, \"·\"]];\nshapesScan = Flatten[Table[If[b == 0, {a}, {a, b}], {a, 1, 4}, {b, 0, a}], 1];\ncScan = Range[-6, 2];\n{tScan, scan} = AbsoluteTiming[With[{o = Om1[zT, wT], c0 = Om2[zT, wT], Z = DiagonalMatrix[zT]},\n    Table[locClass[covT[λ, thN[[1]] + cc hN, Z, c0], o], {λ, shapesScan}, {cc, cScan}]]];\nhits = Select[Flatten[Table[{shapesScan[[i]], cScan[[j]], scan[[i, j]]}, {i, Length[shapesScan]}, {j, Length[cScan]}], 1], #[[3]] === \"SITE 1\" &];\nColumn[{Grid[Join[{Prepend[(\"c = \" <> ToString[#] &) /@ cScan, \"λ \\\\ u = θ1 + c h\"]}, MapThread[Prepend, {scan, ToString /@ shapesScan}]], Frame -> All],\n  Grid[{{\"nontrivial site-1 hits {λ, c}\", hits[[All, 1 ;; 2]]}, {\"time (s)\", tScan}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"942214\" data-output-id=\"64\" data-out-n=\"679\" data-sub-idx=\"8\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"25\" data-sub-start=\"15\" data-sub-end=\"16\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[679]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"26\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:22.88em;vertical-align:-11.19em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:11.69em;\"><span style=\"top:-13.69em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.29em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.29em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:11.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:18em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-8.75em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:9.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mord\"> </span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\"> u = </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class